The GetKeyedService method is not in the ServiceCollectionExtensions.cs file. It might be an extension method from another namespace or a helper method in the project. Since the method is private static in the OptionsOverrides class, I cannot call it directly in tests. I will test the public method GetProviderClusterOptions which calls GetOverridableOption internally.

To test the fallback to GetRequiredService, I will mock IServiceProvider to return null for GetKeyedService and a valid IOptions<ClusterOptions> for GetRequiredService. I will also test the case where GetKeyedService returns a non-null ClusterOptions.

I will create a test class with two tests:
- One where the keyed service is found and returned wrapped in Options.Create.
- One where the keyed service is not found and the fallback GetRequiredService is called.

I will use Moq to mock IServiceProvider and IOptions.

